From 9aff97712d49f6cdfabc2ff7d2f6c6deb5915b73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:54:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Accept JWT bearer tokens on the admin GraphQL endpoints

The admin and domain admin GraphQL endpoints accept only static
passwords. A new 'jwt' listener option makes them also accept
'Authorization: Bearer <token>', verified with configured keys:

- 'keys' is a list of keys with an optional 'kid', tried in order, so
  the signing key can be rotated without redeploying the callers.
  With RS/ES algorithms the server holds only the public key.
- The 'exp' claim is required, 'iss' and 'aud' are checked when
  'issuer' and 'audience' are configured.
- On the domain admin endpoint, the 'domain' claim (configurable with
  'domain_key') names the domain, which has to exist. The token holder
  gets the same permissions as a domain admin with a password.
- The passwords keep working. On the admin endpoint, configuring 'jwt'
  enables authentication like 'username' and 'password' do.
- The option is rejected on the user endpoint, which authenticates with
  the auth methods of the user's host type (e.g. auth.jwt).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
